# NetBird setup key — baked into the V1.2-clean OS image at
# /usr/share/ga-netbird/setup-key (mode 0600). Read by
# /usr/libexec/ga-netbird-register on first boot to register the
# device with NetBird's management plane (api.netbird.io).
#
# To use:
#   1. Get a *reusable* setup key from the NetBird admin panel
#      (Settings → Setup keys → "Create setup key" → reusable, no expiry,
#      auto-group "v12-clean-fleet" or similar).
#   2. Save the UUID below as secrets/netbird-setup-key.txt (no .example).
#   3. Build OS — post-build/88-netbird-setup-key.sh injects it.
#
# IMPORTANT — secrets/netbird-setup-key.txt is gitignored.
# Treat the key as confidential: anyone with it can register peers
# into our network. Rotate via the admin panel if leaked.
#
# Format: single UUID line (uppercase), no surrounding whitespace.
XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX
